          "distinct": true,
          "id": "e6f7500bae94e8140fcfcded610c55d8ad44d01a",
          "message": "build(deps): adopt duckdb 2.0.0 semantics (#376)\n\n## Summary\n\nUpgrade the DuckDB oracle, CLI and matching TPC extensions to 2.0.0,\nwith the lockfile regenerated by pixi 0.81.0. Adopt the changed behavior\nin antb1's supported SQL subset: numeric literal typing and decimal\nconversion/precision, zero-division errors, bottom-up arithmetic\nrewrites and cast preservation, variance, regex replacement validation,\nparser rules, and nested set-operation typing.\n\nFor example, integer division or decimal remainder by zero now raises an\nerror instead of returning NULL. Regression tests cover these changes,\nSQL expectations are regenerated from DuckDB 2.0, and the TPC-DS query\nfingerprint manifest is refreshed. Existing workload pass baselines are\nunchanged.\n\nThe SQL contract documents the remaining rare exceptions: BIGNUM\nfloating-point comparisons, outer qualified stars outside the\nimmediately enclosing WHERE/ON EXISTS form, and established differences\nin error-evaluation timing.\n\n## Type of change\n\n- [x] feat: new SQL, CLI or engine capability\n- [x] fix: bug fix\n- [ ] perf: performance improvement\n- [x] refactor, test, docs, build, ci or chore\n- [x] Breaking change (SQL semantics); labeled `breaking-change`\n\n## Verification\n\nRun locally on macOS arm64 with pixi 0.81.0:\n\n```text\n$ pixi run fmt\nPASS\n\n$ pixi run slt-complete\nPASS; no completion errors\n\n$ pixi run check\nFAIL: existing ShellCheck SC2218\n\n$ SHELLCHECK_OPTS='--exclude=SC2218' pixi run check\nlint: PASS\n443 passed, 2 skipped\n100% tests passed out of 4264\n\n$ pixi run tidy\nPASS\n\n$ pixi run ci-gcc\nUnavailable locally: the gcc environment supports linux-64, while this host is osx-arm64\n\n$ pixi run release\n100% tests passed out of 4265\n\n$ pixi run asan\nFAIL during test discovery, before test execution:\nAddressSanitizer: 64 byte(s) leaked in 1 allocation(s)\n```\n\nThe temporary SC2218 exclusion was explicitly approved by the\nmaintainer; no repository lint configuration is changed. Debug/release\ncounts include the existing pending window-function canary. Both runs\ninclude the TPC workload checks.\n\nThe ASan failure recurs outside the sandbox. Its allocation stack is\nlibdispatch/CoreFoundation, reached by Arrow's Azure dependency calling\n`Curl_macos_init` during static initialization. The failing plan-test\nbinary does not link DuckDB, and Arrow/Azure/curl lock entries are\nunchanged. No sanitizer suppression was added. Linux `check-full`\nremains for CI.\n\nThe compatibility fix (`a5ff8b4`) passes `pixi run fmt`, `pixi run\ntidy`, and the full local `check` command with the approved SC2218\nexception. It resolves GCC's copied structured-binding warning and\ntidy's arithmetic-parentheses, else-after-return, and optional-access\ndiagnostics. Optional-presence assertions remain in place; no compiler\nwarnings or static-analysis checks are disabled. Both [Linux\nclang-tidy](https://github.com/ydb-campus/antb1/actions/runs/44085896584/job/134048113084)\nand [GCC\ncompatibility](https://github.com/ydb-campus/antb1/actions/runs/44085896584/job/134048113294)\npassed on that commit; GCC passed all 4264 registered tests.\n\nThe same CI run exposed an intermittent oracle-test failure: DuckDB 2.0\ncan report either failing UNION branch even with one thread. The\ntest/documentation follow-up (`0f6f073`) preserves antb1's written-order\nassertion, adds its reverse-order case, and checks addition and\nmultiplication separately against both engines with only one failing\nbranch per query. D30 now describes that observed variability. No\ngenerated result blocks changed, and the C++ sources are unchanged from\nthe commit that passed tidy and GCC.\n\n```text\n$ pixi run slt-complete\nPASS; no generated result blocks changed\n\n$ pixi run test -R '^(slt|oracle)\\.setops\\.union\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Local `check` passes with the explicitly approved SC2218 exclusion described above\n- [x] Unit, integration and SQL logic tests cover the changes\n- [x] SQL contract and testing documentation updated\n- [x] No ClickBench data, query answers or values committed\n- [x] No TPC query text, data, answers or tools committed; only the existing fingerprint manifest is refreshed\n- [x] Dependency manifest and lockfile changes approved by the maintainer\n\n## AI assistance\n\n- [ ] No AI assistance\n- [x] AI-assisted: Codex implemented the migration, regenerated expectations, ran checks and reviewed the diff with a reviewer agent.\n- Accountable human: pending maintainer review; no human review is claimed.\n --repeat until-fail:20\nPASS; 20 antb1 runs and 20 DuckDB runs\n\n$ pixi run fmt\nPASS\n\n$ SHELLCHECK_OPTS='--exclude=SC2218' pixi run check\nPASS; lint: 443 passed, 2 skipped; 100% tests passed out of 4264\n```\n\nCI is rerunning on `0f6f073`; its results are pending.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Local `check` passes with the explicitly approved SC2218 exclusion\ndescribed above\n- [x] Unit, integration and SQL logic tests cover the changes\n- [x] SQL contract and testing documentation updated\n- [x] No ClickBench data, query answers or values committed\n- [x] No TPC query text, data, answers or tools committed; only the\nexisting fingerprint manifest is refreshed\n- [x] Dependency manifest and lockfile changes approved by the\nmaintainer\n\n## AI assistance\n\n- [ ] No AI assistance\n- [x] AI-assisted: Codex implemented the migration, regenerated\nexpectations, ran checks and reviewed the diff with a reviewer agent.\n- Accountable human: pending maintainer review; no human review is\nclaimed.",
