          "distinct": true,
          "id": "885dc194f88f7832389331564b5ad2b2df9dbfd8",
          "message": "feat(sql): support correlated in and not in conjuncts (#381)\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements the first half of SQ8c from ADR 0037: keyed correlated `IN`\nand `NOT IN` conjuncts in WHERE and inner ON, including computed\ncorrelation keys, selected expressions, DISTINCT, grouping, HAVING, and\nstatic aggregates.\n\nThe dependent plan keeps the membership pair separate from the\ncorrelation. IN becomes a semi join. Equality-correlated NOT IN uses\nseparate hash lookups for matching values and per-binding row/NULL\ncounts, preserving NULL-probe and empty-set behavior without scanning\nevery pair in a correlation bucket. Static aggregates retain their\nempty-input value and distinguish a NULL item from a row removed by\nHAVING.\n\nSelected expressions run after the required correlation filtering,\nincluding risky aggregate arguments. FULL JOIN placement rejects invalid\ncorrelated membership before column resolution. Exact-domain evaluation\nthat would clone pending correlated subqueries, free outer references,\nor LIMIT remains explicitly unsupported until SQ9.\n\nAdds 38 regression records covering error evaluation, NULLs, empty sets,\nand DuckDB's DISTINCT behavior. A synthetic 240-row disjoint-membership\nprofile falls from 57,600 candidate pairs to 240.\n\nUpdates the SQL contract, adds DuckDB-completed synthetic SQL tests and\nrandomized membership generation, and verifies execution plus all\nEXPLAIN entry points. The second SQ8c PR covers nested correlated\npredicates. Later roadmap shapes (including correlated membership marks\nand per-binding value selection by LIMIT/OFFSET) retain explicit\nunsupported tests.\n\n## Type of change\n\n- [x] feat: new SQL, CLI or engine capability\n- [ ] fix: bug fix\n- [ ] perf: performance improvement\n- [ ] refactor, test, docs, build, ci or chore\n- [ ] Breaking change (CLI, output format or semantics)\n\n## Verification\n\n```text\n$ mkdir -p /private/tmp/antb1-381-check-tmp\n$ TMPDIR=/private/tmp/antb1-381-check-tmp TEST_TMPDIR=/private/tmp/antb1-381-check-tmp SHELLCHECK_OPTS='--exclude=SC2218' pixi run check\n100% tests passed out of 4276\n(existing pending window-function canary skipped)\n\n$ pixi run tidy\nPASS\n\n$ ANTB1_DIFF_SEED=381 pixi run diff-random\nDIFF: PASS seed=381 queries=2000 failed=0 unsupported=0\n\n$ pixi run slt-complete\nPASS; expected results generated by DuckDB\n```\n\nThe check uses the previously approved local SC2218 workaround; no lint\nsettings are changed. Each worktree uses its own temporary directory to\navoid collisions in existing test fixtures. Linux GCC compatibility is\nleft to CI.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] `pixi run check` passes locally (with the approved SC2218\nworkaround above)\n- [x] Tests cover the change\n- [x] SQL behavior documentation updated\n- [x] No ClickBench-derived data committed\n- [x] No TPC-H/TPC-DS query text, data, answers, or tools committed\n- [x] Governance paths unchanged\n\n## AI assistance\n\n- [x] AI-assisted: Codex implemented the changes, generated expectations\nthrough DuckDB, ran validation, and performed an advisory code review.\n- Accountable human: maintainer review pending.",
