          "distinct": true,
          "id": "7f6853e3e549bb413cf0d9a090860217a32bd680",
          "message": "feat(sql): execute whole-partition aggregate windows (#385)\n\n## Summary\n\nExecute W2 whole-partition aggregate windows over surviving raw rows and\ngrouped output, including `OVER ()` and inline `PARTITION BY`\nexpressions. The dedicated Window operator consumes its upstream once,\nshares compatible grouping, finalizes aggregates in bounded chunks, and\ngathers results back to each input row under the query memory budget.\nLater window slices remain Unsupported across execution and every\nEXPLAIN mode, including unused CTEs.\n\nPreserve FLOAT provenance through window MIN/MAX, retain optimizer and\nruntime-filter barriers, and add allocation-failure/cancellation tests,\nDuckDB-completed SLTs, serial/parallel and metamorphic coverage, CLI\ngoldens, and an independent W2 random stream. The maintainer approved\nexactly six ratchet additions: Q12, Q20, Q53, Q63, Q89 and Q98, taking\nthe queries derived from TPC-DS from 84/99 to 90/99. ClickBench and\nTPC-H ratchets, the recursive canary, dependencies and ADR status are\nunchanged.\n\nImplements W2 from ADR 0043, following #384.\n\n## Type of change\n\n- [x] feat: new SQL, CLI or engine capability\n- [ ] fix: bug fix\n- [ ] perf: performance improvement\n- [ ] refactor, test, docs, build, ci or chore\n- [ ] Breaking change (CLI, output format or semantics)\n\n## Verification\n\nLocal platform: macOS arm64, locked pixi 0.81.0 environments. Commit:\n`ac581ef`.\n\n| Command | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `pixi run slt-complete` | PASS; expectations generated by DuckDB and\nreviewed |\n| `ANTB1_UPDATE_GOLDENS=1 pixi run test -L cli` | PASS, 147/147\nincluding fixture setup |\n| `pixi run ci` | PASS, 4,323/4,323; existing permanently pending\nrecursive-canary skip |\n| `pixi run tidy` | PASS after fixing all new findings, without\nexclusions |\n| `pixi run coverage` | PASS on final source, all module floors |\n| `pixi run check` | FAIL: ShellCheck SC2218 in unchanged scripts;\nformatting and all other hooks pass, tooling tests 443 passed / 2\nexisting skips |\n| `pixi run check-full` | FAIL at lint; the remaining local legs were\nrun individually; GCC requires Linux |\n| `pixi run asan` | FAIL before tests, during GoogleTest discovery:\n64-byte leak in CoreFoundation/libdispatch initialization via\nlibcurl/libazure; reproduced outside the sandbox |\n| `pixi run fuzz-smoke` | FAIL after completing 200,000 inputs: 56-byte\nlibFuzzer `StartRssThread` / libc++ thread leak at exit; reproduced\noutside the sandbox; corpus replay passes |\n\nThe ShellCheck diagnostics are in `scripts/agent-setup.sh`,\n`scripts/static-sources.sh` and `tools/github/apply-settings.sh`. No\nsuppression, gate relaxation, dependency change or ADR status change is\nincluded.\n\nThe maintainer explicitly approved opening this draft despite the\ndocumented local ShellCheck and macOS sanitizer failures. This exception\nis limited to draft creation; all CI and merge requirements remain in\nforce.\n\n[PR CI](https://github.com/ydb-campus/antb1/actions/runs/44414798947)\nhas passed Linux lint, GCC (4,323 tests), coverage/fuzz smoke,\nClickBench (43/43), and macOS release. Linux ASan and clang-tidy also\npassed; `CI OK` is green. The [branch\nCI](https://github.com/ydb-campus/antb1/actions/runs/44413603874), on\nthe exact same commit, completed with green `CI OK`, including Linux\nASan and clang-tidy. Static, CodeQL, and PR title checks have passed.\n\nThe [Nightly\nrun](https://github.com/ydb-campus/antb1/actions/runs/44413650789) has\npassed Linux ASan SF1, ASan data tests, Linux arm64 release/data tests,\nthe 20,000-query differential run, long fuzzing, shuffled tests, and all\nthree cold static builds. Its ThreadSanitizer job failed in DuckDB's\nParquet reader/writer and allocator during oracle tests (131 failures);\nthe [latest main-branch TSan\njob](https://github.com/ydb-campus/antb1/actions/runs/44295930602/job/134772821607)\nhas the same failure signatures (133 failures). W2's exec/plan/engine\nunit tests passed under TSan. This failure remains recorded, without\nsuppression or a blind rerun. The full static test suite also passed.\nAll other Nightly test jobs passed; the Nightly workflow remains failed\nbecause of TSan.\n\n### Workload cost validation\n\nScale factor 1, Linux x86-64, from the **PR's `gcc-compat` (`pixi run\nci-gcc`)** [workload-cost\nsummary](https://github.com/ydb-campus/antb1/actions/runs/44414798947/job/135192143436),\ncommit `ac581ef`.\n\n| Query | Total seconds | antb1 seconds | Peak query memory (MiB) |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Q12 | 0.606 | 0.448 | 4.8 |\n| Q20 | 0.808 | 0.451 | 5.6 |\n| Q53 | 2.466 | 1.873 | 3.4 |\n| Q63 | 3.329 | 2.575 | 3.4 |\n| Q89 | 2.606 | 2.234 | 5.7 |\n| Q98 | 2.483 | 1.828 | 6.0 |\n\nAll six matched DuckDB at scale factors 0.1 and 1. Every newly answered\nquery is below the approximately 1.5 GiB memory gate. The slowest GCC\nSF1 shard took 101.0 seconds, 12% of its 870-second inner timeout, below\nthe approximately 60% gate.\n\n[Linux `pixi run\nasan-tpc-sf1`](https://github.com/ydb-campus/antb1/actions/runs/44413650789/job/135188117705)\nalso passed all eight SF1 shards plus fixture setup. Its slowest shard\ntook 391.0 seconds (45% of 870 seconds), and the six new queries used\n3.4–6.0 MiB peak query memory. No workload timeout or memory gate was\nrelaxed.\n\nThis workload is derived from the TPC-DS Benchmark and is not comparable\nto published TPC-DS Benchmark results, as this implementation does not\ncomply with all requirements of the TPC-DS Benchmark.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] `pixi run check` passes locally (lint + clang Debug -Werror +\nhermetic tests)\n- [x] Tests cover the change\n- [x] Docs updated where behavior or architecture changed\n- [x] No ClickBench-derived data is committed (ADR-0006)\n- [x] Nothing derived from TPC-H or TPC-DS is committed: no query text\nor fragments, data, answers or TPC tools (ADR-0006)\n- [x] Protected ratchet change agreed with the maintainer: only the six\nentries above\n\n## AI assistance\n\n- [ ] No AI assistance\n- [x] AI-assisted: Codex implemented the feature, generated oracle\nexpectations, ran verification, and performed an advisory reviewer-agent\naudit. Review findings received regressions and fixes.\n- Accountable human: maintainer review is still required; no human\napproval is claimed.",
