          "distinct": true,
          "id": "4b9665cf69acc08c10128a2c2ea9696f4c178cde",
          "message": "feat(sql): execute running rows window aggregates (#387)\n\n## Summary\n\nExecute W4 running aggregate windows with explicit `ROWS UNBOUNDED\nPRECEDING` and `ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW`. Typed\nprefix kernels cache argument-array pointers before traversal and carry\nstate across batches, reset at partition boundaries, share ordered\nlayouts with RANK, and validate results before emitting output. They\ncover the existing non-DISTINCT aggregate family over raw rows, grouped\noutput and successive query blocks, with query-budget accounting and\ncleanup on failure.\n\nAdd operator, engine, CLI, DuckDB-completed SQL logic, metamorphic and\nindependent random-generator coverage. Ordered aggregates with omitted\nframes and other deferred window forms retain their existing refusals.\n\nWith maintainer approval, add only Q51 to the TPC-DS-derived ratchet\n(98→99), update the SQL contract, and mark W1–W4 Built in ADR 0037.\n\n## Type of change\n\n- [x] feat: new SQL, CLI or engine capability\n- [ ] Breaking change\n\n## Verification\n\nAll local commands used pixi 0.81.0 on macOS arm64.\n\n| Command | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `pixi run ci` | PASS: 4,352 tests, including SF 0.1, parallel SF 0.1\nand all SF 1 ratchet shards after the approved update |\n| `pixi run coverage` | PASS: 4,348 tests and every module floor; 96.67%\nlines, 90.59% branches overall |\n| `pixi run tidy` | PASS |\n| `pixi run test -R 'RandomValidAsts' -j 1 --repeat until-fail:3` |\nPASS: all four seed cases and the aggregate coverage case, each repeated\nthree times |\n| `pixi run test -R 'Window\\|window'` | PASS: 91 tests after the P2 fix,\nincluding memory-budget and allocation-failure coverage |\n| `pixi run test -R '^(sql\\|plan\\|exec\\|engine\\|cli)\\.'` | PASS: 3,005\ntests on the isolated rerun |\n| `ANTB1_DIFF_SEED=20261119 ANTB1_DIFF_COUNT=3000 pixi run diff-random`\n| PASS: 3,000 compared, no failures or unsupported results |\n| `pixi run slt-complete` | PASS: expectations generated by DuckDB for\n22 new W4 records; the two existing W4 records leave pending status |\n| `ANTB1_UPDATE_GOLDENS=1 pixi run test -L cli` | PASS: 151 tests; two\nnew goldens reviewed |\n| `pixi run fmt` | PASS |\n\nThe P2 follow-up caches each call's argument arrays once across output\nranges and capacity retries, with pointer storage charged to the query\nbudget. Prefix kernels receive array-pointer spans, eliminating per-row\n`RecordBatch::column()` locking and reference counting. The expanded\nchunk-boundary regression covers COUNT, MIN and MAX arguments, NULLs and\npartition resets. Full CI, coverage and clang-tidy were rerun after this\nchange; coverage passes every floor. Sanitizer and fuzz failures below\nwere reproduced again outside the sandbox.\n\nThe Linux ASan [run on\n`2e29659`](https://github.com/ydb-campus/antb1/actions/runs/44537579018/job/135606984117)\ntimed out only in `sql.ParserPropertyTest.RandomValidAstsRoundTrip` at\n120 seconds; the window tests passed. That test now registers one case\nper existing seed, retaining all four streams, 300 iterations per seed\nand every round-trip assertion. A separate case retains the original\naggregate generator-coverage checks. Timeouts, corpus size and coverage\nfloors are unchanged. All 4,352 local CI tests and clang-tidy pass after\nthe split. The Linux ASan result for the new commit is pending.\n\nLocal gate failures remain visible:\n\n- `pixi run check` and `pixi run check-full`: existing ShellCheck SC2218\nfindings in unchanged scripts; other lint hooks and 443 tooling tests\npass. `check-full` stops at lint, so the available macOS legs were run\nindividually.\n- `pixi run asan`: a 64-byte CoreFoundation/libdispatch leak during test\ndiscovery, reproduced outside the sandbox and matching the previous W3\nrun.\n- `pixi run fuzz-smoke`: all 200,000 runs and corpus replay complete,\nbut LeakSanitizer reports 56 bytes from libFuzzer's `StartRssThread`,\nalso reproduced outside the sandbox and matching W3.\n\nThis draft is opened at the maintainer's request after disclosure of\nthese local failures. Linux CI, human approval and resolved review\nthreads remain required. No checks or merge requirements are weakened.\n\n### Workload validation\n\nQ51 matches DuckDB at SF 0.1 and SF 1, including parallel SF 0.1. As a\nlocal macOS dev diagnostic, its SF 1 engine time was 6.670 s with 73.2\nMiB peak query memory. These are results of queries derived from TPC-DS,\nnot TPC Benchmark results; this implementation does not comply with all\nrequirements of the TPC-DS Benchmark.\n\nLinux `gcc-compat` SF 1 costs must replace the local diagnostic in the\ncompletion record when CI finishes. Linux `asan-tpc-sf1` validation is\nstill pending.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] `pixi run check` passes locally\n- [x] Tests cover the change\n- [x] Docs updated where behavior changes\n- [x] No ClickBench-derived data is committed\n- [x] No TPC-derived query text, data, answers or tools are committed\n- [x] Protected ratchet and roadmap changes explicitly approved by the\nmaintainer\n\n## AI assistance\n\n- [x] AI-assisted: Codex implemented W4, generated oracle expectations,\nran verification, and used a read-only reviewer agent.\n- Accountable human review: pending; AI review is advisory.",
